    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_31b5e9b42d4f1ca6e7f112c5bcee86b61a33ffaa76a1195d140d0a5d94d91616",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "After the Perron residues are separated into an inverse-logarithmic main cluster and remote scale classes, the remote-residue problem is reduced to a signed exponent inequality. A bipartite graph converts near-equalities of directed shift differences into connected components whose squared signed weights give a strict positive exponent gap; equivalence classes of near-parallel deviations then generate nested graphs that propagate such gaps through the ordered intermediate scales and close the required small-o comparison.",
