    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4b6f03f3e6629a53dd33b1cfb2eb4f8ef288840e5cf3d48c0fad42b5e5c439f6",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The paper encodes the same pairwise displacement at three linked levels: matrix-size rescaling makes N|alpha| the characteristic-polynomial correlation coordinate, the prime-polynomial coefficient norm is capped when oscillation begins beyond the inverse shift, and the coefficient Euler product places conjugate zeta singularities at the corresponding shift differences. With N identified with log(T/2pi), these representations jointly explain why inverse-logarithmic separation is the transition scale.",
