      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b4f0232373b67df289f9ee5f6bb3850242c02f26f11737733ff2bf4afbec7287",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under RH, the upper-bound proof converts the weighted shifted zeta product into a tail problem for an additive sum of shifted log absolute values, majorizes that sum by two prime-polynomial blocks, compresses the short block's pairwise oscillatory coefficient energy into W, and optimizes high moments to obtain tail decay that layer-cake integration turns back into the moment bound.",
