    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d575b5e74f9c101a995e271010a8c7319899e723351c25ba7180d5d5e6b42d4e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the unconditional lower bound, a short Dirichlet polynomial is used as a witness for the shifted zeta product. Its mean square becomes positive diagonal coefficient energy, multiplicativity expresses that energy through displaced zeta factors, and Fourier localization recovers the same diagonal inside the smoothed target-witness correlation; Cauchy-Schwarz then transfers the correlation-to-energy ratio to the desired zeta moment.",
