    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_fecdf8aecbe6ddda2ec337a5376d046a7aaf705ca6a084cc1acccf60dcbb87da",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Both calculations handle collision before decomposing singular contributions. In the matrix contour, rescaling merges the two pole families when N|alpha| tends to zero; at finite scaled separation the determinant and Vandermonde denominator are regularized jointly by divided differences. In the Dirichlet-series calculation, zero and every inverse-logarithmically close displaced pole are enclosed by one small contour and their leading Laurent parts are extracted as a cluster.",
